{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "Field mappings shared by every logs-* data stream on this platform",
    "managed_by": "sentinel-platform",
    "design_notes": {
      "mappings": "dynamic:false is the single most important setting here. Logs contain attacker-controlled keys; with dynamic mapping on, one request carrying 5000 unique JSON keys creates 5000 fields and the cluster state grows until the master node falls over. Unmapped fields are still stored in _source and remain visible in the document, they are just not indexed.",
      "mappings.properties.labels": "labels is the one place dynamic mapping is allowed, because it is where the application puts its own fields. Everything under it is mapped on first sight; keep it to low-cardinality values.",
      "mappings.properties.blockchain": "ECS has no blockchain field definitions, so this namespace is a local extension. Field names mirror the concepts real consensus clients expose (slot, epoch, validator index, reorg depth, peer id) so that grok parsers for Lighthouse or Prysm output could target the same schema later. Every field here is queried by at least one BC-* detection rule; with dynamic:false an unmapped field is stored but not indexed, and a rule querying it would silently never fire."
    }
  },
  "template": {
